# Document Archive Rules

## Core Principles

- Documents are split into two categories: long-lived state documents and record documents.
- Long-lived state documents keep stable paths and describe current requirements, design, verification, tasks, knowledge, and rules.
- Record documents must have IDs and archive by year and month so directories do not become unbounded flat lists.
- Record document IDs use `TYPE-YYYYMMDD-NNN`, where `NNN` is a 3-digit sequence for the same type on the same date.
- Record documents must be listed in the corresponding index so commits, audits, releases, and archives can reference them.

## Long-Lived State Documents

Long-lived state documents do not use global record IDs by default:

- `docs/workflow/00-intake/README.md`
- `docs/workflow/01-requirements/README.md`
- `docs/workflow/02-design/README.md`
- `docs/workflow/03-implementation/README.md`
- `docs/workflow/04-verification/README.md`
- `docs/workflow/05-tasks/README.md`
- `docs/knowledge/context/README.md`
- `docs/knowledge/structure/README.md`
- `docs/knowledge/behavior/README.md`
- `docs/knowledge/reference/README.md`
- `docs/rules/*.md`

If a long-lived document family grows too large, split it by feature module:

```text
docs/knowledge/behavior/
  README.md
  auth.md
  billing.md
  notification.md
```

After splitting, keep the directory-level `README.md` as the index and navigation entry.

## Record Documents

Record documents include:

- `CHG`: one change workspace
- `BUG`: bug record
- `ISS`: issue, risk, blocker, or technical debt
- `CR`: change request
- `ADR`: architecture or major technical decision

ID format:

```text
TYPE-YYYYMMDD-NNN
```

Examples:

```text
CHG-20260624-001
BUG-20260624-001
ISS-20260624-001
CR-20260624-001
ADR-20260624-001
```

## Archive Paths

Change workspaces:

```text
docs/changes/active/CHG-20260624-001-commit-rules/
docs/changes/completed/2026/06/CHG-20260624-001-commit-rules/
docs/changes/legacy/2026/06/CHG-20260624-001-commit-rules/
```

Issues, bugs, risks, and technical debt:

```text
docs/issues/open/ISS-20260624-001-doc-numbering/
docs/issues/resolved/2026/06/ISS-20260624-001-doc-numbering/
docs/issues/legacy/2026/06/ISS-20260624-001-doc-numbering/

docs/issues/open/BUG-20260624-001-login-timeout/
docs/issues/resolved/2026/06/BUG-20260624-001-login-timeout/
```

Change requests:

```text
docs/changes/requests/open/CR-20260624-001-new-export-flow/
docs/changes/requests/resolved/2026/06/CR-20260624-001-new-export-flow/
```

ADRs stay flat by default; archive by year when volume grows:

```text
docs/adr/ADR-20260624-001-doc-id-strategy.md
docs/adr/2026/ADR-20260624-001-doc-id-strategy.md
```

Releases continue using version numbers:

```text
docs/releases/v0.2.0.md
```

## Index Requirements

Record documents must be added to the matching directory `README.md` index:

```text
| ID | Title | Status | Path | Related Docs | Created | Updated |
```

Minimum requirements:

- `docs/changes/README.md` indexes every active / completed / legacy change
- `docs/issues/README.md` indexes every open / resolved / legacy issue, bug, risk, and technical debt item
- `docs/adr/README.md` indexes every ADR
- `docs/releases/README.md` indexes every release
- `docs/archive/README.md` indexes every retired or migrated document

## Commit Links

Commit bodies must reference record document IDs and paths:

```text
Change: CHG-20260624-001 / docs/changes/active/CHG-20260624-001-commit-rules/
Issue: ISS-20260624-001 / docs/issues/open/ISS-20260624-001-doc-numbering/
ADR: ADR-20260624-001 / docs/adr/ADR-20260624-001-doc-id-strategy.md
```

If no record document exists, do not replace it with a verbal note. Create the record first, then commit.
